From a7e53294917ad9ef83a99b384a7ac2c1f7caaa58 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 17:08:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] After the vote: going live needs only the flag and the
 four steps (U11 review)

Setting "live": true and running the four publishing steps broke 15 tests in
five files: the U11 tests assumed the committed flag was false, two U17 tests
counted every weekly row as one of the 72, and the year map moved every week
before the pins.

- family-year: before the rotation epoch (counted backward) a pinned week
  keeps its slot, so a pin, or a strand going live under one, changes that
  week and no other. Going live now changes exactly November 8 and 15, 2026;
  the week of November 1 no longer changes under a family mid-week.
- family-world.test.ts and world.test.tsx run the hidden and live cases on
  copies with the flag set for them, and check the committed index against
  whichever way the flag is committed.
- family-index.test.ts and familyTable.test.ts count the Foundations rows
  (a live strand's rows sit beside them).

Verified both ways: hidden as committed, and live with the four steps run
(full pnpm test, every content gate).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JuCQ8kZ25i9zRwNgk6bh4e
